  "final_message": "The bug was in `due_for_retry` in `billing/dunning.py`, and I've fixed it. The 24 existing tests pass, but I didn't add a test for this case or run mypy.\n\nThe filter was `status == \"open\" or (next_attempt_at is not None and next_attempt_at <= now)`. Because of operator precedence, every open invoice counted as due on every billing run, whatever its scheduled retry time. I changed the `or` to `and`, so an invoice is only retried once its `next_attempt_at` has arrived.\n\nI also wrote `answer.json` in the repository root:\n\n```json\n{\"file\": \"dunning.py\", \"function\": \"due_for_retry\"}\n```",
